title: API: Site information
role: manual
tags: #api #manual #zettelstore
syntax: zmk
created: 20220304164242
modified: 20261109130758

Zettelstore can be configured to suit your personal needs.
For example, you can configure the [[''site-name''|00001004020000#site-name]] or the [[default language|00001004020000#lang]].
A user may override the language configuration or the [[''home-zettel''|00001004020000#home-zettel]] by specifying the appropriate key-value pairs in the [[user zettel|00001010040200]] (see also: [[Runtime configuration data that may be user specific or zettel specific|00001004020200]]).

The zettel containing the [[runtime configuration|00001004020000]] is not available to all users in all situations.
For example, if [[authentication is enabled|00001010040100]] and the current user is not authorized as an [[owner|00001010070200]], the runtime configuration cannot be read by the authenticated user.

To retrieve some important data, send an HTTP GET request to the endpoint ''/x'' with the query parameter ''data=site-info''.

Authentication for this request is optional.
If authentication is enabled and the current user is authenticated, the request will be handled using that user's credentials.

```sh
# curl 'http://127.0.0.1:23123/x?data=site-info'
("Zettelstore Manual" "en" "00001000000000" "en")
```

* The first string contains the site name.
* The second string holds the default language.
* The identifier of the home zettel is stored in the third string.
* The fourth string contains the currently active language.

If authentication is disabled, the second and fourth strings have the same value.
They may differ only if a user is authenticated and has chosen to override the language setting.

==== HTTP Status codes
; ''200''
: Retrieval was successful.
  The response body contains an appropriate site info object.
; ''400''
: The value of the query parameter ''data'' is unknown.